  "finding": "Older pending idle completion replaced the newer failed explicit Open reason. Both clean and protocol-failed completion reproduced before implementation at a fixed Index clock.",
  "change": [
    "Persist one monotonic attemptRevision on metadata records, with legacy default zero; use an immediate SQLite transaction for conditional observation. No attempt history or transcript is stored.",
    "Bind active startup, confirmation, worker-loss, idle-exit and shutdown writes to their last owned revision. Explicit refusal observes unconditionally and advances the revision; stale lifecycle writes cannot take it back.",
    "Preserve actual cleanup, slot release, drain and separate index-failure diagnostics independently of the latest UI attempt. Internal revisions are omitted from the unchanged public DSH schemas."
  ],
  "regressions": [
    "Both clean and uncertain idle completion preserve SESSION_WORKER_DRAINING after completion at the same clock; actual exit is retained and a fresh explicit Open can acquire the released slot.",
    "Retired startup completion cannot overwrite a newer prelaunch refusal after directory revocation and owned-worker cleanup.",
    "Stale observation is rejected after closed/failed/closed at an identical timestamp and SQLite reopen; the latest observation can still write.",
    "Idle completion keeps its actual exit/index-failure diagnostic and releases the worker slot during a real Index directory-replacement fault."
  ],
